@TITLE Pirate Adventure
@AUTHOR Adapted from Scott Adams
@START flat
@DESC_TEXT Treasure hunt from London to a pirate island.

@ROOM flat
@DESC
Your tiny London flat. Rain
streaks the window. A dusty
bookshelf sags under old
volumes. Crackers sit on the
table beside cold tea.
A leather-bound book catches
your eye on the top shelf.
@ENDDESC
@ITEM crackers "Crackers" "Stale ship's biscuits. Something might eat these."
@CHOICE "Read the old book" -> flat_book
@CHOICE "Go outside" -> docks

@ROOM flat_book
@DESC
The cracked leather cover reads
"Voyages of Doubloon." Inside,
faded ink tells of a pirate
captain who buried his plunder
on a nameless tropic isle. A
folded map slips from the
spine and flutters to the floor!
@ENDDESC
@ON_ENTER @SET know_treasure
@SCORE +5
@CHOICE "Pick up the map" -> flat_with_map

@ROOM flat_with_map
@DESC
The map is yellowed and salt-
stained. An island is drawn in
ink with an X marked deep in
the interior. Longitude and
latitude are scrawled along the
edge. Your heart pounds.
@ENDDESC
@ITEM treasure_map "Treasure Map" "Shows Captain Doubloon's island at 18N 64W."
@CHOICE "Head to the docks" -> docks

@ROOM docks
@DESC
London docks. Fog rolls off the
Thames. Ships creak at anchor,
rigging clanking in the wind.
A sailor's shop huddles between
warehouses. A weathered brig
called the Salty Dog is moored
at the end of the quay.
@ENDDESC
@CHOICE "Enter the shop" -> dock_shop
@CHOICE "Board the ship" -> ship_deck
@CHOICE "Go home" -> flat

@ROOM dock_shop
@DESC
A cramped shop reeking of tar
and tobacco. Ropes, lanterns,
and nautical charts crowd every
surface. A bottle of rum and a
rusty shovel lean by the door.
The shopkeep snores behind the
counter.
@ENDDESC
@ITEM rum "Bottle of Rum" "Dark Caribbean rum. Warms the belly."
@ITEM shovel "Shovel" "Rusty but sturdy. Good for digging."
@CHOICE "Return to the docks" -> docks

@ROOM ship_deck
@DESC
The deck of the Salty Dog.
Salt-crusted planks, coiled
rope, and a brass ship's wheel.
The anchor chain drops into the
murky Thames. A hatch leads
below deck.
@ENDDESC
@CHOICE "Raise the anchor" -> anchor_up_room
@CHOICE "Go below deck" -> ship_hold
@CHOICE "Set sail" -> open_sea @NEED has_anchor_up
@CHOICE "Return to docks" -> docks

@ROOM ship_hold
@DESC
Below deck. Dusty cargo crates
and hammocks sway with the
tide. A parrot in a rusty cage
squawks and ruffles its green
feathers. It eyes you with one
bright black bead.
@ENDDESC
@CHOICE "Give crackers" -> ship_hold_parrot @NEED crackers @USE crackers @SET has_parrot
@CHOICE "Go up on deck" -> ship_deck

@ROOM ship_hold_parrot
@DESC
The parrot snatches the crackers
and gobbles them down. It hops
from the cage onto your shoulder
and nuzzles your ear. "Pieces
of eight!" it squawks happily.
You have a new companion.
@ENDDESC
@ON_ENTER @GIVE parrot
@SCORE +10
@CHOICE "Go up on deck" -> ship_deck

@ROOM anchor_up_room
@DESC
You haul on the rusty chain,
muscles burning. Link by link
the anchor rises dripping from
the Thames. The ship rocks free
of her mooring. The Salty Dog
is ready to sail.
@ENDDESC
@ON_ENTER @SET has_anchor_up
@SCORE +5
@CHOICE "Back to the wheel" -> ship_deck

@ROOM open_sea
@DESC
Open ocean! The English coast
fades astern. For days the wind
is fair. Then black clouds boil
on the horizon. A terrible
storm bears down on you, waves
high as houses. The ship groans
and shudders.
@ENDDESC
@CHOICE "Drink rum for courage" -> storm_survived @NEED rum @USE rum
@CHOICE "Ride out the storm" -> storm_death

@ROOM storm_death
@DESC
A monstrous wave crashes over
the bow. The mast snaps like a
twig. Water fills the hold. The
Salty Dog rolls over and sinks
beneath the churning Atlantic.
A stiff drink might have
steadied your nerves.
@ENDDESC
@GAMEOVER "The storm took you. Liquid courage was the answer."

@ROOM storm_survived
@DESC
You take a long pull of rum.
Fire fills your belly and
steadies your hands. You lash
the wheel and ride out the
tempest. Dawn breaks golden.
An island shimmers on the
horizon like a green jewel.
@ENDDESC
@ON_ENTER @SET storm_done
@SCORE +10
@CHOICE "Sail to the island" -> island_beach

@ROOM island_beach
@DESC
White sand. Palm trees sway
in warm breeze. Crystal water
laps the shore. Your ship rides
at anchor in the cove. Dense
jungle rises inland. Rocky
cliffs jut to the east.
@ENDDESC
@CHOICE "Enter the jungle" -> jungle_path
@CHOICE "Follow the shore" -> rocky_shore
@CHOICE "Climb the cliffs" -> cliff_lookout

@ROOM jungle_path
@DESC
Dense tropical jungle. Vines
thick as your arm hang from
towering trees. Parrots flash
bright in the canopy above.
The air is thick and hot.
@IF has_parrot
Your parrot squawks and bobs
its head, pointing deeper in.
@ENDIF
@ENDDESC
@CHOICE "Follow the parrot" -> pirate_camp @NEED has_parrot
@CHOICE "Hack through vines" -> jungle_lost
@CHOICE "Go back to beach" -> island_beach

@ROOM jungle_lost
@DESC
You slash at vines but they
close behind you. Every path
looks the same. Hours pass in
green twilight before you
stumble back to the beach,
scratched and exhausted.
A guide might help.
@ENDDESC
@CHOICE "Return to the beach" -> island_beach

@ROOM pirate_camp
@DESC
An abandoned pirate camp! A
fire pit full of cold ashes,
rotting hammocks strung between
palms, and rum bottles strewn
about. In the ashes you find a
rusty key. An old logbook
mentions a cave on the shore.
@ENDDESC
@ITEM rusty_key "Rusty Key" "Encrusted with ash. Fits a large lock."
@ON_ENTER @SET found_camp
@SCORE +10
@CHOICE "Head back" -> jungle_clear

@ROOM jungle_clear
@DESC
The parrot knows the way now.
It guides you swiftly through
the tangle of vines and back
toward the shore. Good bird.
@ENDDESC
@CHOICE "Go to the beach" -> island_beach

@ROOM rocky_shore
@DESC
Jagged volcanic rock along
the coast. Waves crash and
spray. A dark cave mouth is
blocked by fallen boulders.
Tide pools glimmer between
the rocks further along.
@ENDDESC
@CHOICE "Clear the boulders" -> cave_entrance @NEED shovel @SET rocks_cleared
@CHOICE "Explore tide pools" -> tide_pools
@CHOICE "Go back to beach" -> island_beach

@ROOM tide_pools
@DESC
Beautiful pools teeming with
tiny fish and bright anemones.
Among the shells you spot a
glass bottle sealed with wax.
A scrap of paper curls inside.
@ENDDESC
@CHOICE "Read the note" -> bottle_note
@CHOICE "Go back" -> rocky_shore

@ROOM bottle_note
@DESC
The note is written in shaky
hand: "The cave holds two
prizes for those bold enough
to look past the first. Seek
the passage behind the chest."
Signed, "A Repentant Mate."
@ENDDESC
@SCORE +5
@CHOICE "Go back" -> rocky_shore

@ROOM cliff_lookout
@DESC
High on the cliffs, wind in
your hair. The whole island
spreads below. Jungle canopy,
white beach, your ship tiny
in the cove.
@IF found_camp
Below the cliffs you can just
make out the dark cave mouth
on the rocky shore.
@ENDIF
@ENDDESC
@SCORE +5
@CHOICE "Climb back down" -> island_beach

@ROOM cave_entrance
@DESC
You lever boulders aside with
the shovel, grunting with the
effort. Cool air rushes from
the dark cave mouth. It smells
of salt and something old.
@ENDDESC
@SCORE +10
@CHOICE "Enter the cave" -> cave_tunnel
@CHOICE "Go back" -> rocky_shore

@ROOM cave_tunnel
@DESC
A winding tunnel, slick with
moisture. Water drips from
stalactites. Your footsteps
echo in the dark. The passage
forks ahead: left drops down,
right curves upward.
@ENDDESC
@CHOICE "Go left" -> cave_trap
@CHOICE "Go right" -> treasure_cave
@CHOICE "Go back" -> cave_entrance

@ROOM cave_trap
@DESC
Dead end! The floor crumbles
beneath your feet. You grab
the rocky ledge as a pit yawns
below. Sharpened stakes gleam
in the darkness far beneath.
@ENDDESC
@CHOICE "Pull yourself up" -> cave_tunnel
@CHOICE "Let go" -> cave_trap_death

@ROOM cave_trap_death
@DESC
You lose your grip and plummet
into the spiked pit below.
Captain Doubloon was not kind
to uninvited guests. Perhaps
the right path was the right
path.
@ENDDESC
@GAMEOVER "A spiked pit ends your quest. Right was right."

@ROOM treasure_cave
@DESC
A vast chamber glittering by
the light of phosphorescent
moss. In the center sits an
ancient iron chest with a huge
rusted padlock. Scratch marks
surround the keyhole.
@ENDDESC
@CHOICE "Unlock the chest" -> chest_opened @NEED rusty_key @USE rusty_key
@CHOICE "Force the lock" -> chest_trap
@CHOICE "Go back" -> cave_tunnel

@ROOM chest_trap
@DESC
You smash at the lock with a
rock. A hidden mechanism clicks
and a poison dart fires from
the chest lid, striking your
neck. Doubloon booby-trapped
his treasure well. You needed
the right key.
@ENDDESC
@GAMEOVER "Booby-trapped! You needed the key from the camp."

@ROOM chest_opened
@DESC
The rusty lock falls away. You
throw open the lid. Gold coins
cascade like a waterfall!
Doubloons, pieces of eight, and
a jewel-encrusted cutlass lie
within. Captain Doubloon's
legendary hoard!
@ENDDESC
@ITEM gold_doubloons "Gold Doubloons" "Hundreds of gold coins stamped with skull and bones."
@ITEM jeweled_cutlass "Jeweled Cutlass" "A curved blade set with rubies and emeralds."
@SCORE +25
@CHOICE "Look behind chest" -> treasure_deeper
@CHOICE "Head for the ship" -> return_beach

@ROOM treasure_deeper
@DESC
Behind the chest, a narrow
crack in the cave wall. You
squeeze through into a hidden
chamber beyond. The air here
is ancient and still.
@ENDDESC
@SCORE +10
@CHOICE "Explore the chamber" -> secret_chamber
@CHOICE "Go back" -> return_path

@ROOM secret_chamber
@DESC
A domed grotto lit by crystals
in the ceiling. On a stone
pedestal sits a golden crown
set with a massive black pearl.
The Crown of Captain Doubloon
himself! The greatest prize of
all.
@ENDDESC
@ITEM pirate_crown "Pirate Crown" "Gold crown with a black pearl. Priceless."
@SCORE +30
@CHOICE "Return to the cave" -> return_path

@ROOM return_path
@DESC
You squeeze back through the
crack, pockets heavy with
plunder. The phosphorescent
moss lights your way through
the winding tunnel and out
into the island sunshine.
@ENDDESC
@SCORE +10
@CHOICE "Head for the ship" -> return_beach

@ROOM return_beach
@DESC
Back on the white sand beach.
Your ship bobs in the cove,
waiting faithfully. The hold
is ready for treasure. The
wind is fair for England.
@IF has_parrot
Your parrot squawks "Home!
Home! Pieces of eight!"
@ENDIF
@ENDDESC
@CHOICE "Board and set sail" -> sail_home

@ROOM sail_home
@DESC
You load the treasure aboard
and raise the anchor. Sails
fill with warm trade wind. The
island shrinks behind you as
the Salty Dog points her bow
toward London. Weeks pass
under clear skies.
@ENDDESC
@SCORE +20
@CHOICE "Arrive in London" -> victory

@ROOM victory
@DESC
The Thames! London's grey
skyline appears through the
fog. You dock at the same
quay you left from, hold
bursting with pirate gold.
From a tiny flat to a
fortune beyond dreams.
@ENDDESC
@SCORE +20
@WIN "You return to London rich beyond measure! Score: {score}"
